I just found out that bows are not two-handed weapons, which means you
can #twoweapon with them! This is particularly awesome for Samurai, who
can wield their katana in one hand, and have the bow ready for instant
firing in the other. Unfortunately this seems to limit the number of
arrows fired to one. I don't know if this is a bug, or another way to
limit the effectiveness of twoweaponing.

Twoweaponing two bows works too, but doesn't appear to offer any
advantage. Obvious YANI: John Woo bows, for d8 arrows fired per turn.

